[O]|cffffcc00Fish to 150:|r with the Expert book read, fish the Booty Bay harbour toward 150 (cap 225) whenever you wait on something here [SK Fishing 150] [G27.4,77.2 Stranglethorn Vale]

[OC]|cffffffffStone of the Tides (optional)|r  -  Baron Revilgaz's chain: two round trips to the haunted isle up the west coast (20.8,23.2, about 54 map units north of town), a bracer collection there, a trip to Dalaran, then Duncan's blade; the last step (Gazban) is on the way to the dungeon. 14,185 XP in all and the Robe of Crystal Waters. Skip the whole block if you are 34 and want the dungeon now
[O]At [TAR773 Krazek], [QA616 The Haunted Isle] (285 XP) [G26.9,77.2 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]At [TAR2496 Baron Revilgaz], [QT616] [QA578 The Stone of the Tides] (2,850 XP: find the haunted island) [G27.2,76.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[OC]Lesser Water Elementals (level 36-37, 24 spawns) cover the isle. Gazban (level 40) and the Altar of the Tides at 25.0,23.6 are for the last quest of the chain: leave them for now. Brinescale Skirmishers (36-38) walk the coast. The Drowned City cave is close by, at about 21.4,27.9
[O]Head north up the west coast to the haunted isle and explore it [QC578] [G20.8,23.2 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]At [TAR2496 Baron Revilgaz], [QT578] (2,850 XP + 40s) [QA601 Water Elementals] (6 Water Elemental Bracers from the isle's elementals) [G27.2,76.9 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]Kill [TAR691 Lesser Water Elemental] on the haunted isle for 6 Water Elemental Bracers [QC601] (~36% - budget ~17 kills) [G20.9,23.3 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]Not 6 bracers after ~17 kills: abandon Water Elementals, and the rest of the chain with it [QS601] [G20.9,23.3 Stranglethorn Vale]
[O]At [TAR2496 Baron Revilgaz], [QT601] (2,850 XP + 40s) [QA602 Magical Analysis] (1,400 XP: the Bag of Water Elemental Bracers goes to Archmage Ansirem in Dalaran) [G27.2,76.9 Stranglethorn Vale]

[OC]|cffffffffDalaran (optional, only with Magical Analysis)|r  -  a flight to Southshore, the ride to the Dalaran crater in the Alterac Mountains, then the hearth back to Booty Bay. It is also the only pass by Archmage Timear before the run
